CORE libcxx
ranges_find.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++ --object-bits 12 --unwind 8
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ find: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body of system-header function
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) std::ranges::find on an int array.  With <ranges> included
CBMC took int * for a segmented iterator: the join_view specialization of
__segmented_iterator_traits matched although its requires-clause cannot be
substituted (N5008 [temp.constr.atomic]/3), so the call went to
__find_segment_if, whose body was dropped.
